From 27de7c1e6e965aa2490f7a85b76f56d02507c45c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:56:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Bluetooth: MGMT: remove the mesh advertising instance
 when done

mesh_send_done_sync() only disables advertising when hdev->adv_instances
is empty, but the instance a mesh packet is advertised through
(le_num_of_adv_sets + 1) is itself on that list and nothing removes it,
so for a mesh transmission the check is never true and advertising is
never disabled here. On the legacy advertising path the controller
keeps advertising the packet and the stale instance stays scheduled for
1000 seconds (hci_schedule_adv_instance_sync() arms adv_instance_expire
with adv->remaining_time, the 1000 the instance was added with); with
extended advertising the set stays enabled until the duration the
controller was given ends. Before the list check was added the disable
was unconditional, which is what the tools/mesh-tester cases
"Mesh - Send cancel - 1/2" have expected since 2022 and now time out on.

Tear the instance down the way Remove Advertising does, with
hci_remove_advertising_sync(): on the legacy path this drops the
instance, cancels its timer and reschedules the next instance if there
is one; with extended advertising it disables and removes that set
only, so other advertising sets keep running, which is what the list
check was added for. The existing list_empty() check then disables
advertising only when no other instance is left. The hand-over to the
next pending packet stays behind the tear-down, under hdev->lock, so a
Mesh Send arriving while the controller commands are in flight is
queued and started once, in order. The request is accounted for even if
the teardown fails; recovery of a residual advertising instance is not
handled here.

The tear-down happens when the done work fires; this patch does not
change when that is.

All removal paths end in mgmt_advertising_removed(). The mesh instance
is internal - Add Advertising rejects instances above
le_num_of_adv_sets, Read Advertising Features hides them and no
Advertising Added is ever sent for them - so skip the event for it
instead of announcing to userspace the removal of an instance it never
saw.

Fixes: f3cb5676e5c1 ("Bluetooth: MGMT: mesh_send: check instances prior disabling advertising")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/mgmt.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
index b19ab17ff1b3..e7da34dbbad5 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
@@ -1123,6 +1123,18 @@ static void mesh_next(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 static int mesh_send_done_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data)
 {
 	struct mgmt_mesh_tx *mesh_tx;
+	u8 instance = hdev->le_num_of_adv_sets + 1;
+
+	/* The packet was advertised through the mesh-only instance
+	 * (le_num_of_adv_sets + 1). Tear it down the way Remove Advertising
+	 * does: with extended advertising this disables and removes that set
+	 * only, otherwise the instance is dropped and the next one, if any,
+	 * is rescheduled. It has to go before the list_empty() check below,
+	 * which the instance itself would otherwise keep false. Account for
+	 * the request even if teardown fails. Recovery of a residual
+	 * advertising instance is not handled here.
+	 */
+	hci_remove_advertising_sync(hdev, NULL, instance, true);
 
 	if (list_empty(&hdev->adv_instances))
 		hci_disable_advertising_sync(hdev);
@@ -1305,6 +1317,13 @@ void mgmt_advertising_removed(struct sock *sk, struct hci_dev *hdev,
 {
 	struct mgmt_ev_advertising_removed ev;
 
+	/* Mesh transmissions use an internal instance (le_num_of_adv_sets + 1)
+	 * above the range Add Advertising accepts and Read Advertising
+	 * Features lists; no Advertising Added was ever sent for it.
+	 */
+	if (instance > hdev->le_num_of_adv_sets)
+		return;
+
 	ev.instance = instance;
 
 	mgmt_event(MGMT_EV_ADVERTISING_REMOVED, hdev, &ev, sizeof(ev), sk);
-- 
